Client Interview Questions

Project: Database Management System for Historical Records

1. Project Overview & Purpose

Who will be the primary users of this system (e.g. historians, staff, students, external researchers)?

What is the main purpose of the system: research, public viewing, internal record-keeping, or a combination?

Will the application be used online, offline, or both?

Any preference for IDE used.

How would you like the html page to be run 


2. Database Requirements – Staff Database

What information should be stored for each staff member? (e.g. name, role, years worked, department, biography, photograph)

Are any fields mandatory or optional?

Should staff records be searchable by: Name, Role, Date range, other criteria?


Database Requirements – Sources Database

What types of sources will be stored? (e.g. books, documents, logbooks, photographs)

What information is required for each source? (e.g. title, author, date, location, reference number)

Should sources be searchable by category, date, or keyword?

Do sources need to link directly to scanned images or external files?

Will users need to see a preview or thumbnail of images?


4. Images Folder & Hyperlinks

What categories should be used for the Images folder? (e.g. Books, Documents, Images, Logbooks)

Are there naming conventions that must be followed for image files?

Should images open in the same page or a new browser tab?

Are there any restrictions on image size or format?


5. User Interface & Navigation

How should users navigate between the 25 pages (menu, buttons, page numbers)?

Should all pages share a consistent header and footer?

Are there branding requirements (logos, colours, fonts)?

Are accessibility features required (e.g. readable fonts, contrast, simple layout)?

Is there any colour schemes, fonts , text colour you’d prefer to be used.

Which pages are mandatory

What would you like each page to display


6. Search & Functionality

Should search results appear on the same page or a new page? (redirect?)

Is advanced search required (multiple filters at once)?

Should users be able to sort results (e.g. by date or name)?


7. Reusability & Future Projects

How many future projects are expected to reuse this design?

Which elements should be easily changeable?
(e.g. headers, titles, database names, colour schemes)

Should the system be adaptable without changing database structure?

What level of technical knowledge will future users have?


8. Documentation & Instruction Manual

Who will use the instruction manual (technical staff or non-technical users)?

Should the manual include: Annotated code examples? Screenshots? Step-by-step instructions?

Which parts of the code must not be modified?

Are there any documentation standards that must be followed?


9. Constraints & Deadlines

Is there a deadline for the completed system?

Are there storage or performance limitations?

Are there legal or ethical considerations (e.g. personal data, copyright)?

How will the final system be tested and approved?
